patches.rationale:
Requests the two revocable permissions the backstop and full-screen alarm need. Also ADD these two methods to the class body (place after showWakeUpAlarm at line 836):

  static const int _etaBackstopId = 424242;

  /// G5: (re)arm an OS-scheduled exact alarm that fires at [fireAt] even if the
  /// app process is dead. Idempotent — replaces any previously scheduled backstop.
  Future<void> scheduleEtaBackstop({
    required DateTime fireAt,
    required String title,
    required String body,
  }) async {
    if (isTestMode) return;
    try {
      // Build the absolute instant from UTC now + remaining, so tz.local is
      // irrelevant. Guard against a past/at-now time (fire ~immediately).
      final now = tz.TZDateTime.now(tz.UTC);
      final target = tz.TZDateTime.from(fireAt.toUtc(), tz.UTC);
      final when = target.isBefore(now.add(const Duration(seconds: 2)))
          ? now.add(const Duration(seconds: 2))
          : target;

      const androidDetails = AndroidNotificationDetails(
        'geowake_alarm_channel_v4',
        'GeoWake Alarms (High Priority)',
        channelDescription: 'ETA backstop wake-up alarm',
        importance: Importance.max,
        priority: Priority.max,
        playSound: false,
        fullScreenIntent: true,
        visibility: NotificationVisibility.public,
        category: AndroidNotificationCategory.alarm,
        audioAttributesUsage: AudioAttributesUsage.alarm,
        ongoing: true,
        autoCancel: false,
        enableVibration: false,
      );

      await _notificationsPlugin.zonedSchedule(
        _etaBackstopId,
        title,
        body,
        when,
        const NotificationDetails(android: androidDetails),
        androidScheduleMode: AndroidScheduleMode.exactAllowWhileIdle,
        payload: 'eta_backstop',
      );
    } catch (e) {
      dev.log('scheduleEtaBackstop failed: $e', name: 'NotificationService');
    }
  }

  /// G5: cancel the ETA backstop (call when the real geofence/EKF alarm fires,
  /// or when tracking stops, so the backstop never double-fires).
  Future<void> cancelEtaBackstop() async {
    if (isTestMode) return;
    try {
      await _notificationsPlugin.cancel(_etaBackstopId);
    } catch (e) {
      dev.log('cancelEtaBackstop failed: $e', name: 'NotificationService');
    }
  }

AndroidScheduleMode.exactAllowWhileIdle is the only mode that fires precisely during Doze — critical because a sleeping rider's phone is in Doze. The backstop uses its own notification id (424242) distinct from the live-alarm id (0) so re-arming never disturbs the real alarm.

